Below is a short write-up of what’s happening, the root cause, and a single *SEARCH/REPLACE* patch that forces the start-URL fetch into “true offline” mode (of the two gatherers, the offline gatherer already goes back online too early, so we explicitly re-offine around our start-URL fetch in `start-url.js`).

1) Bug scenario & root cause  
   - During the “offline-start-url” pass, Lighthouse first runs the `offline` gatherer, which calls `driver.goOffline()` in `beforePass` but then immediately calls `driver.goOnline()` in its `afterPass`.  
   - The very next gatherer is `start-url`, which tries to fire a fetch() while “offline”… but it’s now already back online, so it never really goes through the SW or disk cache.  
   - That is why you see all requests with `fromServiceWorker=false` and `fromDiskCache=false`: we never actually turned the network off for that fetch.

2) Fix strategy  
   - In `lighthouse-core/gather/gatherers/start-url.js`, wrap the entire fetch attempt in an explicit `driver.goOffline()` → fetch → `driver.goOnline(...)` sequence.  

3) *SEARCH/REPLACE* patch  
